7:["$","ol",null,{"style":{"paddingLeft":"1.25rem","lineHeight":"1.9"},"children":[["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Cubbon Park Morning Walk"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— CBD / Cubbon Park"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"Over 300 acres of tree cover right in the middle of the city. Show up before 8 AM on a weekday and it's almost meditative — joggers, chess players, and retirees reading newspapers under old rain trees. The park is free, open daily, and massively underrated even by Bangaloreans themselves."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Toit Brewpub"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— Indiranagar"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"One of the original craft beer bars in India and still arguably the best. The Weiss and Witbier on tap are benchmarks. Come for the beer, stay for the thin-crust pizzas. Reserve a table on the terrace if you're going on a Friday evening — it fills up fast."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Lalbagh Botanical Garden"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— Mavalli / South Bangalore"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"Over 240 years old, Lalbagh is Bangalore's finest garden and has more than 1,800 plant species. The glass house (modelled on London's Crystal Palace) hosts flower shows twice a year during Republic Day and Independence Day week — those are genuinely worth planning a trip around."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Sunday Soul Santhe (Flea Market)"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— Various venues, usually Whitefield or JP Nagar"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"Bangalore's most beloved flea market rotates venues but runs almost every Sunday. Indie fashion, vintage finds, food stalls with everything from Korean BBQ to Coorgi pandi curry, live acoustic sets — it's a full morning well spent. Check their Instagram for the current venue before you go."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"MTR (Mavalli Tiffin Rooms) Breakfast"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— Lalbagh Road, South Bangalore"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"Established in 1924, MTR is less a restaurant and more a rite of passage. The rava idli was literally invented here. Expect a queue on weekends but it moves quickly. Order the masala dosa, rava idli, and filter coffee — that's the classic combination."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Nandi Hills Sunrise Drive"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— ~60 km north of Bangalore"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"Leave the city by 4:30 AM, arrive before the sunrise, and watch the clouds sit below you like a white sea. It's about an hour's drive from central Bangalore and entry is nominal. Weekdays are much better than weekends — on Sunday mornings it can get genuinely crowded."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Natrani Open-Air Theatre"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— Hebbala / Sadashivanagar"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"Part of the Ranga Shankara complex, Natrani is an open-air space that hosts some of Bangalore's most interesting experimental theatre, stand-up, and musical performances. Tickets are affordable and the atmosphere is unlike anything else in the city. Check Ranga Shankara's calendar to see what's on."}]]}],"$Le"]}]
8:["$","h2",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1.4rem","fontWeight":600,"margin":"2rem 0 1rem"},"children":"Why Bangalore Always Has Something New"}]
9:["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":"1.8","marginBottom":"1rem"},"children":"The city reinvents itself faster than most. A brewery opens in a converted warehouse in HSR Layout. A pop-up bookstore appears in Indiranagar for exactly one weekend. A birding group quietly does early-morning walks at Hesaraghatta every Saturday. Bangalore rewards the curious — the more you look, the more you find."}]
a:["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":"1.8"},"children":"Bookmark this page and check back — we update it regularly with what's actually worth your time in Bangalore right now."}]
